      "content": "Melanoma can present differently across various skin tones. In lighter skin, melanoma often appears as a clearly defined, dark lesion that can be easily diagnosed using the ABCDE rule. However, in individuals with darker skin, melanomas may present as less pigmented lesions, appearing as brown, red, or even gray patches. It is crucial to look for any new or changing dark, asymmetrically shaped spots on any skin tone.",
